  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nFall has arrived for North and Central Georgia. Conditions will be \nbeautiful through the long term with chances for precipitation \nbeing as close to zero as we can scientifically make them. Temps \nwill be around what we'd expect for the southeast this time of year \nas the long term picks up on Saturday. Temperatures in the mid 80s \nduring the day will fall into the mid 50s during the overnights. \nRelative humidity values will fall below 40% during the afternoon.\n\nAs we approach the second half of next work week, the ridge will \nbegin to break down and southerly flow will begin to pull moisture \nback into the CWA. This will bring chances for thunderstorms back up \nto between 25-35% during the afternoon as well as push high \ntemperatures back towards the 90s.",
